<%# Puts `transaction` into the list on screen at its sorted position: before
    `preceding`, the row just below it, or before the end-of-list marker when
    nothing sorts below it. When that anchor hasn't been loaded yet (the reader
    hasn't scrolled that far), Turbo drops the stream and the row arrives with
    its page instead, so it can never appear twice.
    Known gap, accepted: if a next-page request read its rows before this
    row was committed but renders after this stream was dropped, the row is
    missing until a reload. Closing it would need a client-side queue of
    insertions waiting for their anchors, for a window of milliseconds. %>
<%= turbo_stream.before(preceding ? dom_id(preceding) : "transactions_end", transaction) %>
